	inline constexpr std::array<WordDef, 4> kWords{ {
		WordDef{ "grah", "SLEN", "Flesh", "the cult's old shrine in the Reach", "SLEN. The ground shakes under the Reach. Slenvahrin, the dragon who carried Alduin's first word, circles the cult's old shrine - and the barrow-dead around it grow new flesh to meet you.", "Slenvahrin crashes onto the shrine and burns away to bone. SLEN is silenced: the strength Alduin poured into the dead now runs in you.", "Flesh Remade: every weapon, bow, spell and wonder hits 15% harder.", "wyrm_slen", "Slenvahrin, the Flesh-Wyrm", -140739.0f, 47973.0f, -4353.0f, 148.0f, 35.0f, 1.0f, { 10, 12, 14, 0 }, { 2, 2, 3, 0 }, 3 },
		WordDef{ "dir", "TIID", "Time", "the courtyard of Labyrinthian", "TIID. Under Labyrinthian, the great tomb of Bromjunaar, the dragon cult laid its dead by the thousand. Tiidrah, keeper of the second word, gives them back the years the grave took - and every one of them hears it.", "Tiidrah falls across the courtyard of Bromjunaar. TIID is silenced: the time the dead stole is yours now.", "Borrowed Time: the night's blows hurt you 20% less.", "wyrm_tiid", "Tiidrah, the Time-Wyrm", -23574.0f, 40679.0f, -6478.0f, 186.0f, 40.0f, 1.0f, { 12, 14, 16, 18 }, { 2, 3, 3, 4 }, 4 },
		WordDef{ "lein", "VO", "Undo", "the dragon lair on Mount Anthor", "VO. On the frozen peak of Mount Anthor, Vonahlok - the Undoing - keeps the last of Alduin's words. Where it flies, death itself comes undone, and the dead of the Pale climb the mountain to its call.", "Vonahlok's shout dies on the wind over Mount Anthor. VO is silenced: the Undoing has undone its last.", "The Curse Undone: your magicka returns 50% faster.", "wyrm_vo", "Vonahlok, the Undoing", 95163.0f, 67275.0f, 259.0f, 0.0f, 45.0f, 1.0f, { 12, 14, 16, 0 }, { 3, 3, 4, 0 }, 3 },
		WordDef{ "echo", "ALDUIN", "The World-Eater's Echo", "the summit of the Throat of the World", "The three words are silent, and only their maker is left. On the summit of the Throat of the World, where the Tongues once cast Alduin out of time, his echo still circles - and the dead of all Skyrim answer it one last time. Climb the mountain at night and end the curse.", "The Echo of Alduin breaks apart over the summit and its voice is gone from the world. The Curse of Alduin is broken: the dead of Skyrim sleep, and the nights are only nights again. Alduin himself still lives - and now he has nowhere left to hide but Sovngarde.", "The Curse Broken: the Hall of the Awakened opens beneath High Hrothgar.", "echo_alduin", "The Echo of Alduin", 56044.0f, -47760.0f, 36055.0f, 0.0f, 80.0f, 1.0f, { 12, 14, 16, 18 }, { 3, 3, 4, 4 }, 4 },
	} };
